FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/runtime.rs:298 — `SystemTime::now().duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH).unwrap()` aborts the process on a clock before the epoch instead of returning a Runtime error — reachable from Redblue source via the `random` builtin (same pattern at src/runtime.rs:605, src/runtime.rs:617, src/runtime.rs:630), while `time_now` at src/runtime.rs:424 handles the same failure with `map_err` — replace each `unwrap()` with the `map_err(|e| Error::Runtime(e.to_string(), span))` path `time_now` already uses.
2. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/codegen.rs:172 — `statement()` emits a `STATEMENT_MARKER` NOP for every statement including `export` (whose arm at src/bytecode/codegen.rs:522 emits nothing else), so a module body charges one step per `export`, while src/vm.rs:728 skips `execute_statement` for `export` inside `declare_module` and charges zero — the two engines reach the step budget at different points for the same module program — skip the marker for in-module `export` statements or charge them in `declare_module`.
